Advanced boundary, Green-function and multipole study (@em-static-study: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @electromagnetism, #source "../sources/Classical-Electromagnetism-Fitzpatrick.lingua#r_7NH7AZZH3NZ2FHJ4K5VBT49F6H", #source "../sources/Eletromagnetismo-Classico-Volume-I-IFRN.lingua#r_612RCJJJDNWD62YYPE9410HHVQ", #source "../sources/Electromagnetism-Tong.lingua#r_278NEA0Z85RJZSPXQ8G55E3SR1", #electromagnetism "../study/An-integrated-electromagnetic-system-investigation.lingua#r_1FQW2ASX2WCT3JRXKKP4NB4HSN") { r_7K6DMSWN5GFG0AH1HFEQFYJ6HR
**Read:** [Classical Electromagnetism — Richard Fitzpatrick](../sources/Classical-Electromagnetism-Fitzpatrick.lingua#r_7NH7AZZH3NZ2FHJ4K5VBT49F6H), whole boundary-value, Green-function and multipole chapters; [Eletromagnetismo Clássico, Volume I — Tibério Magno de Lima Alves](../sources/Eletromagnetismo-Classico-Volume-I-IFRN.lingua#r_612RCJJJDNWD62YYPE9410HHVQ), complete book; [Electromagnetism — David Tong](../sources/Electromagnetism-Tong.lingua#r_278NEA0Z85RJZSPXQ8G55E3SR1), all corresponding electrostatic development.

Investigate a finite arrangement of conducting and dielectric objects with a source close enough that a point-dipole approximation is not automatically adequate. Read the complete relevant boundary/Green/multipole chapters of [Classical Electromagnetism — Richard Fitzpatrick](../sources/Classical-Electromagnetism-Fitzpatrick.lingua#r_7NH7AZZH3NZ2FHJ4K5VBT49F6H), the full [Eletromagnetismo Clássico, Volume I — Tibério Magno de Lima Alves](../sources/Eletromagnetismo-Classico-Volume-I-IFRN.lingua#r_612RCJJJDNWD62YYPE9410HHVQ) electrostatics volume and the corresponding advanced [Electromagnetism — David Tong](../sources/Electromagnetism-Tong.lingua#r_278NEA0Z85RJZSPXQ8G55E3SR1) treatment. Work separated-variable and image constructions before moving to the chosen less symmetric geometry.

Derive the continuous problem, prove the applicable uniqueness statement and choose explicit charge/potential conditions. Obtain one analytical limit and one independently formulated numerical solution. Compare surface charge, force, total energy and far multipole coefficients, not only potential contours. Check source singularities, mesh/domain error and the dependence on reference potential.

Vary source distance and material contrast to quantify where the reduced multipole model fails. Explain differences between fixed charge and fixed voltage with the source's energy exchange. Produce derivations, calculation inputs, convergence evidence and a critical account of what can be inferred from a boundary measurement. Defend a surprising result against an alternative geometry or boundary interpretation. This is a sustained potential-theory investigation, with enough detail for another reader to reconstruct its mathematical and numerical reasoning.

**Continue:** [An integrated electromagnetic-system investigation](../study/An-integrated-electromagnetic-system-investigation.lingua#r_1FQW2ASX2WCT3JRXKKP4NB4HSN).

**Return:** [Electromagnetism — charge, fields, matter, waves and physical evidence](../Electromagnetism.lingua#r_5TJPESCTTNAKY66JH2QNQYN1PY).
